  "answer": "This feature request has been made before. Past tickets ask for a PowerToys utility that excludes chosen windows or apps from screen sharing, recording and screenshots using the WDA_EXCLUDEFROMCAPTURE display affinity. The windows stay visible to you but are not captured. The main tracking issue is PowerToys#46333 (\"Privacy Overlay\"), where a proof-of-concept exists. It uses an injected hook DLL, because setting the affinity from another process is blocked even when elevated. The earlier requests, #34950 (\"Window Masking\") and #48566, were closed as duplicates of other issues, so #46333 is the one to follow. No such feature has shipped yet. Please subscribe to #46333 and add a thumbs-up and your Outlook/Teams scenario there. Until it ships, check your screen before sharing, or share a single app window instead of the whole screen."
 },
